### Signature interactions (build all of these)
1. **Playable hero board:** a real chessboard on the home page (chess.js, drag or tap-to-move) where the visitor can play against the built-in engine at an easy level, with a "Reset" and "Show me a famous game" button that auto-plays a short classic game with captions. Fully keyboard-accessible; on small phones it sits below the headline.
2. **"Pawn to Queen" progress track:** used in every form (Details, Check, Confirmed). The pawn advances as fields are completed and promotes to a queen on success with a short sparkle.
3. **Roadmap as a game:** the annual plan is a vertical path of squares; scrolling moves a knight along it; each stop opens a card with the event (integration day, training, championship, team tournament, simultaneous exhibition, national tournament). Past stops are filled in; the next one pulses.
4. **Weekly rhythm board:** Monday and Thursday as two "files" with piece markers for sessions, training and the online tournament.
