## 15. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

- A member's name in any word order, with or without accents, returns "confirmed" and stores a confirmed registration; a non-member sees the friendly popup and a pending registration is stored; an unpaid member sees the fee popup.
- The browser can never read `members`, `registrations` or any application/message table, and never receives the service-role key (verify with the anon key).
- The site works on a phone in French, English and right-to-left Arabic, in light and dark themes.
- The home page has a playable chessboard; the roadmap, forms and 404 page use the chess interactions listed in section 6.
- A board member can run a 9-round Swiss tournament from Admin and the public page updates live.
- A learner can sign up, study a lesson, miss a quiz question, and see that position return as a spaced-repetition card the next day; progress survives a change of device.
- The whole project deploys from one repo to Vercel free with the Supabase free tier, uses at most 8 serverless functions, and survives a week of inactivity thanks to the keepalive cron.
- Every image on the site is either a labelled dummy placeholder listed in `src/data/images.ts` or one of my two real logos.